From: Abdelhafid DJIDEL <266947999+hafid-logic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:08:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(core): pin balanced surface mapping for random and
 lifecycle

### What
Pins `balanced_surface`: syscall 318 (getrandom) maps to `Random`, `exit`/`exit_group` map to `Lifecycle`, and the console/memory/denied mappings hold.

### Why it matters
The surface table drives the balanced contract's decision. The existing tests check image-read/memory/task arms but not the random or lifecycle arms, so deleting either survives the suite.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| delete `318 => Random` arm | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| delete `SYS_EXIT \| SYS_EXIT_GROUP => Lifecycle` arm | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline (clean tree + new test): PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-core --lib balanced_surface`.

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs
index 5f87a3a..f69f0ef 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs
@@ -934,4 +934,14 @@ mod tests {
             }
         }
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn balanced_surface_maps_random_and_lifecycle() {
+        assert_eq!(balanced_surface(318), BalancedSurface::Random);
+        assert_eq!(balanced_surface(SYS_EXIT), BalancedSurface::Lifecycle);
+        assert_eq!(balanced_surface(SYS_EXIT_GROUP), BalancedSurface::Lifecycle);
+        assert_eq!(balanced_surface(1), BalancedSurface::Console);
+        assert_eq!(balanced_surface(9), BalancedSurface::Memory);
+        assert_eq!(balanced_surface(999), BalancedSurface::Denied);
+    }
 }
